{"step_index":184,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T08:39:24Z","thinking":"**Investigating Tomcat's 400 Errors**\n\nThe `400` status from Tomcat, when proxied by Nginx, warrants examination of what Nginx transmits. Specifically, the Nginx configuration reveals it forwards headers such as `Host`, `X-Forwarded-Proto`, and `X-Forwarded-Ssl`. Potential issues might involve how these headers are processed by Tomcat. Further analysis is required to determine if Tomcat misinterprets the proxied request.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"sshpass -p '8&#JMl1Mwe0GyN' ssh -p 30 -o BatchMode=no -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -o ConnectTimeout=3 superuser@172.30.198.50 id 2>&1 || true","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Test SSH to 172.30.198.50 with superuser"}}]}
