{"step_index":190,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T08:40:18Z","thinking":"**Investigating Request Headers Differently**\n\nConsidering using a Python script for debugging, but realized a simplified approach might suffice. Initially planned to inspect network traffic directly, then remembered that the target port utilizes TLS encryption, rendering that approach ineffective. Instead, a comparison by checking headers of `curl` requests is warranted.\n\n\n**Analyzing Nginx Request Headers**\n\nExamining the Nginx configuration, observed discrepancies in how the `Host` and `X-Forwarded-Host` headers are set and how the `Forwarded` header is being added. The `map` directives in the Nginx config determine the format of the `Forwarded` header based on the client's IP. This might be relevant to the issue.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"~/.ansible/kssh -u superuser 172.30.198.33 'curl -k -i --resolve map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443:172.30.198.50 https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/centreon-map/ | head -n 20'","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Test direct TLS with resolve"}}]}
