{"step_index":230,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T08:54:17Z","content":"Here is the current status:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Nginx Reverse Proxy: <span style=\"color:green\">**100% Configured & Verified**</span>\n\nThe vhost on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33`) has been updated, syntax-checked, and reloaded. \n\nThe simulated end-to-end test confirms the entire flow is working properly:\n```http\nGET https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/\n--> HTTP/2 301 Moved Permanently\n--> Location: https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/centreon-map/\n\nGET https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/centreon-map/\n--> HTTP/2 401 Unauthorized\n--> Content-Type: application/json;charset=ISO-8859-1\n--> {\"code\":401,\"message\":\"Full authentication is required to access this resource\"}\n```\n* **No more 502 Bad Gateway**: Nginx connects to `https://172.30.198.50:9443` over TLS.\n* **No more 404 Not Found**: Root `/` cleanly redirects to `/centreon-map/` preserving port `:9443`.\n* **Centreon Map is answering**: Tomcat serves the authentication endpoint directly through the proxy.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Crucial Firewall vs DNS Discrepancy\n\nNotice the difference in the 3rd octet between what you mentioned and what was added in DNS:\n\n* **Firewall IP you mentioned earlier**: `109.62.`<span style=\"color:#d4a017\">**62**</span>`.18`\n* **DNS entry returned by `th2-dnsp-mst1`**: `109.62.`<span style=\"color:#d4a017\">**64**</span>`.18`\n\n```text\nmap.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.  IN  A  109.62.64.18\n```\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Please check your firewall configuration:\n> * If the firewall DNAT rule is configured on **`109.62.62.18`**, update the DNS record to `109.62.62.18` (or change the DNAT rule to `109.62.64.18`).\n> * If the DNAT is indeed on **`109.62.64.18`**, make sure the rule and port `9443` security policy are committed.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Testing from External Network\n\n* When testing from **inside the corporate LAN/datacenter**, connecting to the public IP may time out due to a lack of **NAT Hairpinning / Loopback NAT** on the firewall.\n* **Test from an external connection** (e.g. mobile 4G/5G or home connection):\n  ```bash\n  curl -k -i -L https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/\n  ```\n  *(Accept the certificate warning in your browser for now, as the certificate is currently issued for `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`).*","thinking":"**Observing redirection and authentication**\n\nThe initial request resulted in a redirection to a secure HTTPS endpoint. Subsequently, an authentication error (401) was received from the server. This indicates that the reverse proxy is successfully redirecting but the subsequent request requires authentication.\n\n\n**Investigating DNS and Firewall Mismatch**\n\nThe DNS record resolves to `109.62.64.18`, while the intended DNAT configuration uses `109.62.62.18`.  This discrepancy suggests the traffic isn't reaching the intended destination if the firewall configuration is indeed on `.62`. Alternatively, if the firewall is configured on `.64`, the issue could be with firewall security rules, or internal network hairpinning.\n\n\n"}
